cartridge "MATH DUNGEON/COMPUTE'S GAZETTE/1985"

' MATH DUNGEON
' A ColecoVision game based on "Math Dungeon", COMPUTE!'s Gazette,
' January 1985 (one BASIC listing for the Commodore 64 and the VIC-20).
' Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic), 2026, in Amy by
' Amy Bienvenu.
'
' Not a cell-for-cell port: the rules are the original's (read from its
' listing, orig/), the game is built for the ColecoVision: the typed
' adventure commands become the joystick and one button, the dungeon is
' drawn as you explore it, smooth sprites, tiles, sounds and an original
' title tune.
'
' The game: choose a level (1-5). In the forest, walk north to the gate,
' open it, go to the old house and open the milkbox: the note in it holds
' a math question. Answer it right and the door flies open; a trap door
' drops you into the Math Dungeon, a 10 x 10 grid of rooms and hallways.
' Take the light first (you cannot move in the dark). Find the green, blue
' and red doors and the green and blue keys. The green door hides a map
' (it shows the whole dungeon and the monster rooms); the blue door hides
' the red key; the red door is the way out. Monsters jump out of some
' rooms and ask a question: answer right and the monster disappears and
' leaves gold (take it before you leave the room); answer wrong and it
' takes all your gold and transports you somewhere else in the dungeon.
' Your score is the gold you carry out.
'
' From the original (orig/math dungeon.bas): the forest, the gate that
' opens and closes, the house, the milkbox and the note's question, a
' wrong answer sending you back; the trap door and the neon sign with the
' level; the dungeon generator (10 + level random monster rooms, each
' with its whole row and column made of rooms and hallways), the start
' room with the unlit light, the two keys and three doors at random
' rooms, the green door's map, the blue door's red key, the red door out;
' "I'd turn on my light first", "there is a wall there"; the monster's
' question, its gold (1 to 10 x level pieces), the robbery and transport
' to a random room; the questions: + and - on levels 1-2, + - x / from
' level 3, numbers up to 10 x level (5 x level for x and /), negatives
' from level 4 (x, /) and 5 (+), no negative difference up to level 3,
' whole quotients only; all the messages (shortened to two lines).
'
' Liberties:
' - Numeric answers: no keyboard, so the answer is set on a dial with the
'   stick (up/down 1, left/right 10, held to repeat) and given with a
'   button. Only one answer per question: a wrong one has its penalty at
'   once (the original also took one INPUT), and every question is new,
'   so answers cannot be swept. The right answer is shown after a wrong
'   one.
' - The red door asks one last question before it opens (a wrong answer
'   transports you), so the way out cannot be reached without math.
' - Commands become context actions: the stick walks (N, S, E, W), the
'   button does what can be done here (open or close the gate, open the
'   milkbox and read the note, take the light, a key, the map or the gold,
'   unlock a door), or repeats LOOK. GET LIGHT and LIGHT ON are one action;
'   the light stays on (LIGHT OFF, INV and the hidden ALGEBRA teleport are
'   left out; what you carry is always on screen).
' - The dungeon is drawn as you see it: the room you are in and its
'   doorways (the original's LOOK) stay drawn, so you need not map it on
'   paper. Items show once you have been in their room.
' - The start room is a random room of the dungeon (the original could put
'   you in an unconnected cell of solid wall and leave you stuck).
' - Without a home key, play-again is a return to the title.
'
' Controls: either controller. Title: left/right choose the level, up/down
' START, HOW TO PLAY or CREDITS, a button
' starts. Play: the stick walks, a button acts. Questions: up/down change
' the answer by 1, left/right by 10, a button answers.
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128; the
' frame loop is protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI off
' after a wait, display off. Music first in the sound table, effects after;
' the title tune is played once. Own xorshift random numbers.

data MsgD chars
  "YOU ARE IN A DENSE FOREST. A"
  "PATH LEADS NORTH.           "
  "YOU ARE FACING NORTH. A GATE"
  "IS IN FRONT OF YOU.         "
  "YOU ARE FACING NORTH. THE   "
  "GATE IS OPEN.               "
  "THE GATE IS CLOSED.         "
  "                            "
  "OK. THE GATE IS OPEN.       "
  "                            "
  "OK. THE GATE IS CLOSED.     "
  "                            "
  "AN OLD HOUSE. THERE IS A    "
  "MILKBOX BY THE DOOR.        "
  "THE DOOR IS CLOSED.         "
  "                            "
  "THE DOOR IS OPEN.           "
  "                            "
  "A NOTE IN THE MILKBOX HAS A "
  "QUESTION ON IT.             "
  "THE NOTE DISAPPEARS. THE    "
  "DOOR FLIES OPEN WITH A BANG!"
  "THE NOTE BLOWS AWAY. YOU ARE"
  "BACK IN THE FOREST.         "
  "A COLD AND DAMP ROOM. THERE "
  "IS AN UNLIT LIGHT HERE.     "
  "YOU ARE IN A COLD AND DAMP  "
  "ROOM.                       "
  "YOU ARE IN A LONG AND NARROW"
  "HALLWAY.                    "
  "I'D TURN ON MY LIGHT FIRST. "
  "                            "
  "OK. YOU HAVE THE LIGHT. THE "
  "LIGHT IS ON.                "
  "THERE IS A WALL THERE.      "
  "                            "
  "THERE IS A GREEN KEY HERE.  "
  "                            "
  "THERE IS A BLUE KEY HERE.   "
  "                            "
  "THERE IS A RED KEY HERE!    "
  "                            "
  "THERE IS A GREEN DOOR HERE. "
  "                            "
  "THERE IS A BLUE DOOR HERE.  "
  "                            "
  "THERE IS A RED DOOR HERE.   "
  "                            "
  "THE DOOR IS LOCKED. YOU DO  "
  "NOT HAVE THE RIGHT KEY.     "
  "THE DOOR OPENS. THERE IS A  "
  "MAP HERE!                   "
  "THE DOOR OPENS. THERE IS A  "
  "RED KEY HERE!               "
  "OK. YOU HAVE THE KEY.       "
  "                            "
  "OK. YOU HAVE THE MAP. SKULLS"
  "MARK THE MONSTERS.          "
  "A MONSTER JUMPS OUT: 'YOU   "
  "MUST ANSWER THIS QUESTION!' "
  "THE MONSTER DISAPPEARS. YOU "
  "SEE SOME GOLD HERE!         "
  "'NOW I'LL TAKE ALL YOUR GOLD"
  "AND TRANSPORT YOU AWAY!'    "
  "THE RED DOOR ASKS ONE LAST  "
  "QUESTION BEFORE IT OPENS.   "
  "THE RED DOOR SLAMS. A SUDDEN"
  "FLASH AND YOU ARE AWAY!     "
  "THE DOOR IS OPEN.           "
  "                            "
end data
